File Index

/kt-gateway.ts
Purpose: `/ws/kt` authoritative match gateway — `MatchRegistry` (in-memory sessions + subscribers), `handleClientMessage` (socket-free, unit-testable dispatch on `join`/`action`/`requestSnapshot`/`leave`), `setupKtWebSocketGateway` (mounts on an http.Server). Phase F: `join` accepts an optional `token`; `setupKtWebSocketGateway`'s new `resolveAccountId` option (injected, e.g. from index.ts's introspection wiring) resolves it to an accountId BEFORE calling `handleClientMessage` (kept synchronous/testable on purpose) — `resolveAccountId` and its `.catch` are the only place introspection can fail, and failure always means an anonymous join, never an error to the client. `setupKtWebSocketGateway`'s new `onMatchComplete` option fires exactly once per match (guarded by `MatchSession.tryClaimForRecording()`, checked at BOTH places `over` can broadcast — `driveAi` and the `action` case — since either can observe a just-decided match) so a persistence layer can hook in without this file taking on any I/O itself.
